JWT:

A JWT (JSON Web Token) is an open, industry-standard (RFC 7519) compact, URL-safe method for securely transmitting information between parties as a JSON object. It is primarily used for stateless authentication and authorization, allowing servers to verify user identity without storing session data. It consists of three base64url-encoded parts: Header, Payload, and Signature. 

JWT consists of three parts namely:

1. Header
2. Payload
3. Signature.

Header-> JWT type and Algorithm used for signing.
PayLoad-> sub(username to identify the user), roles(Admin/user), permissions, iat, exp,custom claims like permisions, accountstatus or whatever it might be.
Signature-Ensure the token is not modified and not tampered.

HMACSHA256(
  base64(header) + "." + base64(payload),
  secret_key
)

What JWT DOES NOT store
Very important for interviews:
❌ Passwords
❌ Database credentials
❌ Secrets
❌ Refresh tokens
❌ Bank/financial info
❌ Personal sensitive info (Aadhaar, PAN, etc.)


