@PostAuthorize is a Spring Security annotation that runs authorization logic after the method execution.
Unlike @PreAuthorize, which checks conditions before method execution, @PostAuthorize lets you validate the returned object and decide whether the caller should be allowed to see it.
It is mainly used in read‑operations where access decisions depend on the returned resource.

Possible Expression:
@preAuthorise("hasAuthority('WEATHER_READ')or hasRole('Admin')")
For write/update/delete operations → always use @PreAuthorize/

@postAuthorise("returnObject.username==authentication.name" or hasRole('hr')
For read-only use postAuthorise.
