"@PreFilter is used to filter method input before it reaches the business logic. It is especially useful when 
a method accepts a list or collection—Spring Security can automatically remove unauthorized items based on expressions. 
This prevents invalid or unauthorized data from being processed and protects bulk operations, multi‑tenant access, and privilege‑sensitive actions.
For Example:
You're building a REST API that allows bulk update or bulk delete.
User sends:

{
  "ids": [1,2,3,4,5]
}

B ut the logged‑in user may only have permission to modify IDs 1 and 4.
Instead of rejecting the whole request:

@PreFilter(filterObject.owner==authentication.name)

removes unauthorized items
